        "label": "D-1 Cut over the pilot with Postgres logical replication",
        "raw": "/projects/2415ccf7-9c11-4023-b933-f5ab9db037d3/decisions?decision=ed772b25-a0de-45e6-b207-108169f39486",
        "href": "/projects/2415ccf7-9c11-4023-b933-f5ab9db037d3/decisions?decision=ed772b25-a0de-45e6-b207-108169f39486",
        "targetId": "ed772b25-a0de-45e6-b207-108169f39486",
        "resolves": true
      }
    ],
    "answer": "We chose to use Postgres logical replication for the pilot cut-over because application-layer dual-write would have required changes to nineteen write paths in the payments service, taking four to five weeks of work. The benefit of quicker rollback with application-layer dual-write was not needed at pilot volume. This decision was made on 2026-09-09. [D-1 Cut over the pilot with Postgres logical replication](/projects/2415ccf7-9c11-4023-b933-f5ab9db037d3/decisions?decision=ed772b25-a0de-45e6-b207-108169f39486)",
    "finishReason": "stop"
  },
